<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">First Philippine Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1899 CE – 1901 CE · capital Malolos</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Constitutional republic proclaimed at Malolos in 1899, often called the first in Asia, which fought the United States for independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Following the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/revolutionary-government-of-the-philippines">Revolutionary Government of the Philippines</a> and the drafting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos-constitution">Malolos Constitution</a> by a congress of revolutionary delegates, the Philippine Republic was inaugurated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barasoain-church">Barasoain church</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a> on 23 January 1899, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> as president and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apolinario-mabini">Apolinario Mabini</a> as head of the cabinet.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution established a parliamentary system with an assembly, separation of church and state, and civil rights. In practice the war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, which began on 4 February 1899, absorbed all efforts. The government moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-fernando-pampanga">San Fernando</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarlac-city">Tarlac</a> and other towns as American forces advanced, and turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare in late 1899.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Aguinaldo</a> was captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palanan">Palanan</a> in March 1901 and swore allegiance to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>. Generals such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-malvar">Miguel Malvar</a> fought on until 1902. Though defeated, the republic became a foundation of Filipino national identity, and its flag and anthem were later adopted by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-philippine-republic.jpg" alt="First Philippine Republic" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Philippines_(1898%E2%80%931901).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1899 CE – 1901 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Malolos</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Emilio Aguinaldo, Apolinario Mabini</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tagalog, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/philippines">Philippines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Malolos Republic, Philippine Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=first-philippine-republic" aria-label="First Philippine Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7982 1625 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Philippine Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8302 1881L8309 1895M8302 1881L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8309 1895h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8302 1881h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8302 1881h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Malolos. <a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=first-philippine-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
